# Subject: imperative mood, under 72 characters, no trailing period.
# "Add reveal bounds check", not "Added" or "Adding" or "reveal stuff".
#
# Blank line, then the body. The body answers why, not what. The diff
# already says what. If the change is not obvious in six months, say
# what you tried that did not work, or what constraint forced it.
#
# One logical change per commit. If the body needs the word "also",
# that is two commits.
#
# State verification honestly. "Tests pass" means you ran them. If
# something is unverified, say so in the body rather than implying it
# works. An unverified commit is fine. A commit that pretends is not.
#
# Reference the handoff step where relevant, for example "Step 2".
#
# No Co-Authored-By trailers. Commits are authored by the repository
# owner regardless of which tool produced the diff.
